From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Mon, 08 Sep 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: match a channel switch action against the
 receiving link

ieee80211_rx_h_action() compares the BSSID of an extended channel switch
announcement against sdata->deflink.u.mgd.bssid. An MLO association does
not use the default link, so that field holds the zero address and the
frame is never queued.

Use the BSSID of the link the frame arrived on. ieee80211_rx_data_set_sta()
always sets rx->link, and for a non-MLO association it points at the
default link, so this keeps the current behaviour there.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/net/mac80211/rx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/rx.c
@@ -3731,7 +3731,7 @@ ieee80211_rx_h_action(struct ieee80211_r
 			break;
 		if (!rx->sta)
 			break;
-		if (!ether_addr_equal(mgmt->bssid, sdata->deflink.u.mgd.bssid))
+		if (!ether_addr_equal(mgmt->bssid, rx->link->u.mgd.bssid))
 			break;
 		if (mgmt->u.action.action_code !=
 				WLAN_PUB_ACTION_EXT_CHANSW_ANN)
